### InventoryQuery — Phase 2, Query Invocation (run-time)
### Calls published Inventory queries the way an independent client app would.
### Prereqs: inventory-query is running (./dry-run.sh) and publish_query.http has been run, so
### inventory.stockByWarehouseAndStatus is published to ["warehouse_manager", "supply-chain"]
### and inventory.needsRestockByCategory to ["supply-chain", "data_analyst"].

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8082

### Stock lines in Chittagong that are running low.
POST {{baseUrl}}/data-query
Content-Type: application/json
X-Roles: warehouse_manager

{
  "name": "inventory.stockByWarehouseAndStatus",
  "params": { "warehouseId": "WH-CTG", "status": "LOW_STOCK" }
}

### Backordered lines in Khulna, calling as a group.
POST {{baseUrl}}/data-query
Content-Type: application/json
X-Roles: supply-chain

{
  "name": "inventory.stockByWarehouseAndStatus",
  "params": { "warehouseId": "WH-KHL", "status": "BACKORDERED" }
}

### Everything at or below reorder level in PHARMA, by bare query name.
POST {{baseUrl}}/data-query
Content-Type: application/json
X-Roles: data_analyst

{
  "name": "needsRestockByCategory",
  "params": { "category": "PHARMA" }
}

### 403 FORBIDDEN — data_analyst isn't allowed to call the warehouse query.
POST {{baseUrl}}/data-query
Content-Type: application/json
X-Roles: data_analyst

{
  "name": "inventory.stockByWarehouseAndStatus",
  "params": { "warehouseId": "WH-DHK", "status": "IN_STOCK" }
}

### 404 QUERY_NOT_FOUND — Order queries live in order-query, not here.
POST {{baseUrl}}/data-query
Content-Type: application/json
X-Roles: senior_DBA

{
  "name": "orders.ordersByStatusAndBranch",
  "params": { "status": "SHIPPED", "branchId": 12 }
}
